{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Above all the nations which He has made, for a praise, and for a name, and for a glory.</b> The measure of the verse is thus: 'and to set you on high for a praise, and for a name, and for a glory, above all the nations which He has made' — for the idolaters which He made are not given over to praise and to name and to glory, but they are given over to the portion of the stars and the constellations. 'Not so is the portion of Jacob, for He is the former of all things' — this is what it says, 'for a praise and for a name,' for Israel are given over to praise and to His great name: 'for a praise,' in the manner of what is written (Deuteronomy 10:21) ״הוא תהלתך״, and 'for His great name,' and He is your Elohim."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:24.219903386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}